{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Ceuqozz1dUXsNTXgd73gs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Repository Findings\n\n- **Shipment.kt:9-14** — Shipment data class with status field\n- **Shipment.kt:23-27** — ShipmentStatus enum: CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt:15-18** — save() method persists shipments; findById() retrieves by ID\n- **ShipmentController.kt:20-56** — Existing endpoints: POST /shipments (create), GET /shipments/{id}, GET /shipments\n- **ApiExceptions.kt:18-24** — ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) are available\n- **ApiError.kt:31-37** — ErrorCode enum with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- **GlobalExceptionHandler.kt** — Centralizes error response formatting\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to the ApiError envelope\n- ConflictException → 409 status; ResourceNotFoundException → 404 status\n- Tests verify both HTTP status and error code in response body\n- Pattern: repository for persistence, controller for HTTP semantics\n\n## Affected Files\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Must add error code for \"shipment already cancelled\" case (409 conflict)\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test cases for confirm endpoint\n\n## Risks\n\n- Adding a new error code changes the public API contract; it must be deliberate\n- Idempotency: confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment must not fail\n- The confirm endpoint should return 200 OK with the updated shipment, not 201 Created\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone. The requirement is clear: CREATED→CONFIRMED (success), CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED (idempotent success), CANCELLED→error 409, non-existent→error 404.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed Changes**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` error code to the ErrorCode enum. This indicates the shipment is in a terminal state and cannot be confirmed.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Fetch shipment by ID; throw ResourceNotFoundException (404) if not found\n   - If status is CREATED: update to CONFIRMED, save, return 200 with updated shipment\n   - If status is CONFIRMED: return 200 with unchanged shipment (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED: throw ConflictException (409) with SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add tests covering:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change (idempotent)\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with correct error code\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with correct error code\n\n**Alternative Rejected**\n\nI considered not adding a new error code and reusing VALIDATION_FAILED or a generic message, but this violates the API contract principle stated in ApiError.kt: \"error codes are part of the public API; add one deliberately.\" The CANCELLED case is a real state conflict, not a validation error, so it deserves its own code.\n\n**Data and Error Flow**\n\n| Case | Input | Processing | Output | Status |\n|------|-------|-----------|--------|--------|\n| CREATED shipment | shipmentId | Find shipment, update status to CONFIRMED, save | Shipment with status=CONFIRMED | 200 OK |\n| CONFIRMED shipment | shipmentId | Find shipment, status already CONFIRMED, no change | Shipment unchanged | 200 OK |\n| CANCELLED shipment | shipmentId | Find shipment, throw ConflictException | ApiError with code=SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED | 409 Conflict |\n| Non-existent | shipmentId | findById returns null, throw ResourceNotFoundException | ApiError with code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND | 404 Not Found |\n\n**Test Strategy**\n\n- **Test 1**: Confirms a CREATED shipment → verify status changes to CONFIRMED, response is 200 OK, body contains shipment\n- **Test 2**: Confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment → verify status stays CONFIRMED, response is 200 OK (idempotent)\n- **Test 3**: Confirms a CANCELLED shipment → verify response is 409 Conflict, error code is SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED\n- **Test 4**: Confirms a non-existent shipment → verify response is 404 Not Found, error code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the design. First, let me add the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":18470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":617},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1eaeb16-f55f-4a53-a41e-21e9cc437fc4","uuid":"1a1ebfe5-a30e-4ce1-904f-6578cfaeb94b","timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:32:37.535Z","request_id":"req_011CeuqozEMyoEAvpJSnxgG6"}
